# Ownership is deliberately narrow: only .github/ is owned.
#
# A pull request that touches nothing under .github/ is unaffected by this file —
# GitHub requires a code-owner review only on pull requests that modify owned
# paths. Product code keeps its normal single-approval flow.
#
# Why .github/ specifically. Everything that governs how this repository is
# built, scanned and released lives there: the workflow wrappers that call the
# org's reusable workflows, dependabot.yml, and this file. For a `pull_request`
# event GitHub runs the workflow *from the pull request itself*, so a change to
# quality.yml or security.yml gates its own pull request — which means an
# unreviewed edit can weaken the checks that were supposed to catch it.
#
# Either team can approve; both carry write access to every repository in the
# organisation, which CODEOWNERS requires or the entry is silently ignored.

/.github/  @ZySec-AI/org-admins @ZySec-AI/org-maintenance
